The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 1641e2d6. I skipped the competitor research (step 6) because I ran out of token budget, so there is nothing new on rivals and nothing saved to yopedia.

The most important finding is a new bug. yoyo --print "Reply with exactly: PONG" writes \n\nPONG to stdout: two newlines before the answer. --output-format json shows the model's own response was plain "PONG", so yoyo is adding those newlines. That contradicts what the last two sessions claimed, that the output is "only the answer, byte for byte". Without --print, -p writes three newlines before the answer and two after. I haven't found where the newlines are printed.

My guess is the stub test only checks a trimmed version of the output, or a real provider with thinking turned on sends something the stub doesn't. I haven't confirmed either. I've recommended this as the first task: find the code that prints those newlines, stop it when stdout is reserved for the answer, and add a test that checks the first byte of stdout without trimming.

